WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.933 --> 00:00:02.535
-Welcome back to our show.

00:00:02.535 --> 00:00:04.537
Both Brooklyn kids,
so I appreciate you

00:00:04.537 --> 00:00:06.972
coming back on the show.
-My pleasure.

00:00:06.972 --> 00:00:09.575
-How are you feeling?

00:00:09.575 --> 00:00:11.210
-I'm feeling good.
-Yeah.

00:00:11.210 --> 00:00:12.979
-Could feel better.
-Yeah, okay.

00:00:12.979 --> 00:00:14.247
[ Light laughter ]

00:00:14.247 --> 00:00:16.549
Last night probably did not
go as planned.

00:00:16.549 --> 00:00:19.953
-No, it did not.
We won one state.

00:00:19.953 --> 00:00:24.824
We are in the lead in the second
state up for grabs last night,

00:00:24.824 --> 00:00:26.258
the state of Washington,

00:00:26.258 --> 00:00:28.061
with about two-thirds
of the votes cast.

00:00:28.061 --> 00:00:29.829
But we lost some
important states.

00:00:29.829 --> 00:00:32.131
-So where is your head at
right now?

00:00:32.131 --> 00:00:35.535
-Well, my head is at...

00:00:35.535 --> 00:00:40.406
that we have introduced
an agenda, Jimmy,

00:00:40.406 --> 00:00:42.574
that I think the American people
now support.

00:00:42.574 --> 00:00:45.778
And what poll after poll shows
is that people support

00:00:45.778 --> 00:00:48.114
raising the minimum wage
to a living wage.

00:00:48.114 --> 00:00:51.851
People now understand,
especially with the Coronavirus,

00:00:51.851 --> 00:00:54.520
that it is insane
that we live in a nation

00:00:54.520 --> 00:00:57.357
in which 87 million Americans
are uninsured

00:00:57.357 --> 00:01:01.060
or underinsured and can't get to
a doctor when they should.

00:01:01.060 --> 00:01:03.963
That we need a Medicare For All
single payer program.

00:01:03.963 --> 00:01:05.398
People got that.

00:01:05.398 --> 00:01:08.301
People understand that
in this day and age,

00:01:08.301 --> 00:01:11.103
if you are going to make it
into the middle class,

00:01:11.103 --> 00:01:12.471
you need to be able
to go to college,

00:01:12.471 --> 00:01:14.974
regardless of your income,
or go to a trade school.

00:01:14.974 --> 00:01:16.809
That we got to make public
colleges and universities

00:01:16.809 --> 00:01:18.243
tuition free.

00:01:18.243 --> 00:01:21.714
I think people understand that
despite Trump's nonsense,

00:01:21.714 --> 00:01:24.617
climate change is a real,
existential threat

00:01:24.617 --> 00:01:26.019
to our planet.

00:01:26.019 --> 00:01:27.954
We got to take on
the fossil fuel industry.

00:01:27.954 --> 00:01:29.621
We got to transform the country.

00:01:29.621 --> 00:01:33.092
On all of those issues,
we have succeeded, I think,

00:01:33.092 --> 00:01:36.963
in bringing the American people
into a progressive agenda.

00:01:36.963 --> 00:01:40.199
What we have also done, and I'm
enormously proud of this,

00:01:40.199 --> 00:01:43.836
is in poll after poll
and election after election,

00:01:43.836 --> 00:01:46.839
we win the overwhelming majority
of young people.

00:01:46.839 --> 00:01:50.042
The young people of this country
are on our side.

00:01:50.042 --> 00:01:52.945
Truth is, Biden does very,
very well with older people,

00:01:52.945 --> 00:01:54.580
and they vote.

00:01:54.580 --> 00:01:56.649
Young people don't vote as much
as I would like.

00:01:56.649 --> 00:01:58.951
But the future of this country

00:01:58.951 --> 00:02:01.520
believes in
a progressive agenda,

00:02:01.520 --> 00:02:05.191
which says that we need
a government and an economy

00:02:05.191 --> 00:02:08.194
that works for all,
not just a few.

00:02:08.194 --> 00:02:11.598
That we have to overcome
the racism and the sexism

00:02:11.598 --> 00:02:14.100
and the homophobia
and the xenophobia

00:02:14.100 --> 00:02:16.902
and religious bigotry
that we're now experiencing.

00:02:16.902 --> 00:02:19.705
So on all of those issues,
we have succeeded.

00:02:19.705 --> 00:02:22.108
Where we have not succeeded,
frankly,

00:02:22.108 --> 00:02:24.477
is that most people today
think that

00:02:24.477 --> 00:02:27.113
Joe is more electable
than I am.

00:02:27.113 --> 00:02:29.215
So we see people say,
"Oh, we love you, Bernie.

00:02:29.215 --> 00:02:31.083
We love your ideas,
but I'm voting for Joe

00:02:31.083 --> 00:02:33.085
because he's more electable."

00:02:33.085 --> 00:02:34.520
Bet--
-Why?

00:02:34.520 --> 00:02:38.758
Why do you think he's coming
across as more electable?

00:02:38.758 --> 00:02:41.561
-I mean, I think the fact
that he was vice president

00:02:41.561 --> 00:02:43.129
for eight years with Obama,

00:02:43.129 --> 00:02:45.832
and Barack Obama remains
a very popular figure

00:02:45.832 --> 00:02:47.833
within the Democratic world.

00:02:47.833 --> 00:02:51.003
I think that's one thing.

00:02:51.003 --> 00:02:54.840
And I think the media has played
a role in that as well.

00:02:54.840 --> 00:02:57.844
But what I honestly believe --

00:02:57.844 --> 00:02:59.479
and Joe is a friend of mine.

00:02:59.479 --> 00:03:03.349
What I honestly believe is that
in order to defeat Trump,

00:03:03.349 --> 00:03:05.684
we need the largest
voter turnout

00:03:05.684 --> 00:03:07.119
in the history of this country.

00:03:07.119 --> 00:03:09.088
Trump is not going to be
easy to beat.

00:03:09.088 --> 00:03:12.024
And I think you need a campaign
of energy and excitement.

00:03:12.024 --> 00:03:14.627
I think you're going to have to
bring young people

00:03:14.627 --> 00:03:17.564
into the political process
in a way we've not seen before,

00:03:17.564 --> 00:03:21.167
and I think you've got to get
through to working class people,

00:03:21.167 --> 00:03:24.370
who in many cases have given up
on the political process.

00:03:24.370 --> 00:03:25.672
They don't vote anymore.

00:03:25.672 --> 00:03:27.439
They think nobody cares
about them.

00:03:27.439 --> 00:03:29.008
You know, they can't afford
health care.

00:03:29.008 --> 00:03:30.276
Can't afford child care.

00:03:30.276 --> 00:03:31.944
Can't afford to send their kids
to college.

00:03:31.944 --> 00:03:34.213
Is anybody worried about them?
Well, we are.

00:03:34.213 --> 00:03:35.914
But they don't --
they've gone and given up,

00:03:35.914 --> 00:03:38.551
and I think we are the campaign
to bring those folks in.

00:03:38.551 --> 00:03:40.753
-You think we can do that, yeah.
-Yeah.

00:03:40.753 --> 00:03:42.721
-Do you think --
say it is Biden,

00:03:42.721 --> 00:03:44.556
do you think Biden can
beat Trump?

00:03:44.556 --> 00:03:46.625
-I do. I mean, I think,
you know,

00:03:46.625 --> 00:03:50.463
when you have a president
who is a pathological liar.

00:03:50.463 --> 00:03:53.032
[ Whistle, applause ]
When you have a president --

00:03:53.032 --> 00:03:54.867
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:54.867 --> 00:03:56.803
When you have a president

00:03:56.803 --> 00:03:58.738
who truly, apparently
has never read

00:03:58.738 --> 00:04:00.606
the Constitution
of the United States...

00:04:00.606 --> 00:04:01.807
[ Light laughter ]

00:04:01.807 --> 00:04:04.143
...who thinks he is
above the law,

00:04:04.143 --> 00:04:07.513
who is a racist and a sexist
and all of that stuff,

00:04:07.513 --> 00:04:11.817
I think even, you know,
Republicans and moderates

00:04:11.817 --> 00:04:13.085
are going to say,
"You know what?

00:04:13.085 --> 00:04:14.553
We can't have four more years
of this guy."

00:04:14.553 --> 00:04:16.255
So do I think Joe can beat him?
I do.

00:04:16.255 --> 00:04:18.658
You know, between you and me,
don't tell anybody.

00:04:18.658 --> 00:04:20.259
[ Laughter ]

00:04:20.259 --> 00:04:21.527
-Don't worry about it.

00:04:21.527 --> 00:04:23.362
-I think we're the stronger
campaign to do that.

00:04:23.362 --> 00:04:24.730
-Yeah. You think you are.
Yeah.

00:04:24.730 --> 00:04:25.898
-I do.
-What do you think about --

00:04:25.898 --> 00:04:27.666
Are you getting pressure
from the DNC for you

00:04:27.666 --> 00:04:29.702
to step down and drop out?

00:04:29.702 --> 00:04:32.371
-Well, there's been pressure
from day one.

00:04:32.371 --> 00:04:35.441
You know, I think it's
no great secret

00:04:35.441 --> 00:04:38.577
that there was a lot of
nervousness at a time

00:04:38.577 --> 00:04:40.980
when you had people like
Amy Klobuchar

00:04:40.980 --> 00:04:43.783
and Pete Buttigieg
and Bloomberg

00:04:43.783 --> 00:04:46.552
kind of splitting
the more moderate vote.

00:04:46.552 --> 00:04:49.922
So there was an effort to try to
get rid of all of those folks.

00:04:49.922 --> 00:04:51.757
-Because there was also
that stuff,

00:04:51.757 --> 00:04:54.059
Donald Trump has been saying
for at least a month

00:04:54.059 --> 00:04:56.829
that the DNC is trying to squash
the Sanders campaign.

00:04:56.829 --> 00:04:58.731
"They're never going to let him
be the nominee.

00:04:58.731 --> 00:05:00.233
Trust me, folks."

00:05:00.233 --> 00:05:01.834
Do you think the president
is right?

00:05:01.834 --> 00:05:04.536
-What amazes me, here we have
a stock market

00:05:04.536 --> 00:05:06.738
that is collapsing.

00:05:06.738 --> 00:05:11.477
You have a Coronavirus that is
scaring the entire world.

00:05:11.477 --> 00:05:14.780
We have climate change, which is
a threat to the human planet.

00:05:14.780 --> 00:05:17.950
And Donald Trump keeps worrying
about the Democratic primary.

00:05:17.950 --> 00:05:19.819
[ Light laughter ]
So, Mr. President,

00:05:19.819 --> 00:05:21.887
if you watch anything
other than Fox --

00:05:21.887 --> 00:05:24.356
I don't know that you do...
[ Laughter ]

00:05:24.356 --> 00:05:26.625
Why don't you do your job?

00:05:26.625 --> 00:05:28.927
Pay attention to the needs
of the American people.

00:05:28.927 --> 00:05:31.431
Don't worry so much about
the Democratic primary.

00:05:31.431 --> 00:05:33.999
[ Laughter ]
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:33.999 --> 00:05:35.868
-I think he watches.

00:05:35.868 --> 00:05:38.904
I think he watches.

00:05:38.904 --> 00:05:42.274
So you announced today that
you're not stepping down,

00:05:42.274 --> 00:05:44.410
and you are going
to the debate this Sunday.

00:05:44.410 --> 00:05:47.146
-Right.
-And this Sunday -- no audience.

00:05:47.146 --> 00:05:48.714
-No audience, right.

00:05:48.714 --> 00:05:50.649
-How will that affect the way
you do a debate?

00:05:50.649 --> 00:05:51.850
Is that going to be different
for you?

00:05:51.850 --> 00:05:53.019
-It will be different.
I mean,

00:05:53.019 --> 00:05:54.653
all of the other debates,
I think this is like

00:05:54.653 --> 00:05:57.056
the tenth or the eleventh
debate, had audiences.

00:05:57.056 --> 00:05:58.925
But it's okay.

00:05:58.925 --> 00:06:00.960
What is most important --
this is the first debate

00:06:00.960 --> 00:06:02.128
where there are only two people,

00:06:02.128 --> 00:06:03.929
which makes it
a very different debate

00:06:03.929 --> 00:06:05.932
than when you have 8 people or
10 people or whatever.

00:06:05.932 --> 00:06:07.266
-Did you hate those things?
-I did.

00:06:07.266 --> 00:06:09.067
-Those giant debates?
-It was like a food fight.

00:06:09.067 --> 00:06:10.603
You know? And --
[ Light laughter ]

00:06:10.603 --> 00:06:12.404
And everyone's yelling
and screaming.

00:06:12.404 --> 00:06:14.440
And you can't get anything
of substance.

00:06:14.440 --> 00:06:16.809
I think on this debate with
two people in two hours,

00:06:16.809 --> 00:06:18.777
you know what, we are actually
going to be able

00:06:18.777 --> 00:06:23.116
to discuss the issues impacting
the families of America.

00:06:23.116 --> 00:06:25.885
-It's on CNN and Univision,
so everyone tune in for that.

